            "reviewBody": "This salad was a big hit. Nice combination of textures and sweet and tart flavors."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sheila Burns"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I have made this salad for more than 30 years. Banana? No...Chop berries and 1 cup of sugar, and pineapple (drained) the night before you plan to eat it. Let meld in the fridge. In the morning, drain off excess juice (this will make a stiffer salad) and add marshmallows, 1 cup chopped walnuts, and whipped cream (extra stiff). Mix well and keep in the fridge until serving. Will keep up to 1 week if prepared this way.",
            "datePublished": "2015-11-23T13:15:40.960Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sherbear1"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this for Thanksgiving and everyone loved it. The only changes I made were when I put the cranberries in the food processor I added 1/2 cup of heavy whipping cream, I also added 1/2 cup more of sugar. Thanks for the great recipe.",
            "datePublished": "2009-11-27T09:49:19.690Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "millier"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Family loved it for Thanksgiving! It is a bit sweet--next time I will cut back on sugar quite a bit. Also, cranberries come in 12 oz bags around here, not 1 # anymore. I used 1 bag and it was fine, but I really like cranberries and next time may use the 16 oz, especially considering you always discard a few. Still think 1 1/2 C or less of sugar is plenty.",
            "datePublished": "2014-12-22T08:48:10.327Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Rachel"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was a great hit but I made a double batch for our Thanksgiving gathering and with everything else there was way too much. The only thing I would change is using 1 cup or less of sugar. Two cups is way too much.",
            "datePublished": "2016-12-13T23:59:00.820Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "abbeyroad"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I didn't put the banana in this salad. At first I forgot to add the whipping cream and it tasted good not great. The next day I added whipping cream to the rest and it was great!! The fresh cranberries add a great zip and contrast to the sugar.",
            "datePublished": "2010-01-07T05:55:38.293Z"
          },
          {
